Donald Trump's press secretary Kaley  mcenany was asked at her Monday press  briefing by reporters whether Donald  Trump plans to resume the coronavirus  press briefings and she didn't answer  the question but the answer is obviously  no and it's a good question to ask  because we're seeing massive coronavirus  hot spots growing very rapidly in the  United States mostly different areas  than the early hot spots and I'm going  to talk about the virus itself shortly  but there's a real media story here to  understand we talked about the bully  pulpit of corporate media much of what  is in the national discussion the top  three stories that are in the national  discussion at any given time are  essentially led by corporate media and  this is called agenda setting power it's  not necessarily that corporate media  tells us what to think about any  particular issue although sometimes they  do but it's that corporate media tells  us what to think about what to talk  about and I'll give you an example  remember kids in cages the immigration  scandal it's still going on but it's  rarely if ever in the media except to  mention that some people being held at  the border have contracted coronavirus  but nothing has fundamentally changed  about that story which was wall-to-wall  coverage previously during this  administration now it's like it doesn't  exist then it was coronavirus we have a  pandemic daily press briefings including  Donald Trump and doctors pouchy and  Bert's  daily updates down to the specific  details about the number of masks and  project air bridge flights from Mike  Pence and then the White House signaled  we're going to stop Trump wondered aloud  about injecting bleach and isopropyl  alcohol to treat coronavirus it became  clear that the White House didn't really  want more visibility for doctors Burks  and Foudy talking about the virus so the  briefing stopped and with that over time  as more and more states have decided to  reopen some are safely reopening some  are very unsafely reopening the topic of  the virus itself started to take a  backseat especially as the George Floyd  killing took place and the massive  protests started and now as we're seeing  the protests  sir starting to die down a little bit  but the big topic has become defund the  police or do not defund the police  depending on whose perspective you're  listening to right-wing media saying  defunding the police would be anarchy  some on the Left furious that Biden does  not want to defund the police but  understand that nothing materially has  changed with coronavirus we'll look at  the data put it up on the screen now  fortunately as you can see we've seen a  leveling off and a slow decline in the  number of cases at the national level  but mostly what we're seeing is the  cases being relocated where we are  finding new hot spots understand that at  the peak we were finding 25 to 30,000  cases a day we are still finding 19 to  25 thousand new cases every single day  and the number of active cases meaning  people who currently have the virus is  still as high as it's ever been and yet  Donald Trump barely talks about  coronavirus his press secretary barely  talks about coronavirus right-wing media  is done with it other than calling it a  scam or a conspiracy and even corporate  media is increasingly talking about  coronavirus less and less but we have a  new political article that points out  not only is the pandemic still very much  a pandemic with no effective treatment  no vaccine we have new hot spots that  are setting records for new cases there  are parts of the country that are  exploding with virus cases and Donald  Trump is just silent another massive  failure because Trump by not talking  about it makes people think the threat  is over  meaning they go out and behavior  responsibly and cause even more cases  and in fact as we talked about yesterday  on the bonus show Donald Trump is  planning to restart his huge mag or  alleys as part of his 20/20 re-election  campaign in a couple of weeks so I'll  give you some really specific examples  Texas which started to reopen pretty  quickly is exploding week to week they  have more and more cases the number of  active cases in Texas is higher today  than it has ever been  Florida run by Republican governor Ron  de Santos  also started to open pretty early they  were caught lying about numbers as we  previously covered and after a small dip  sometime in April which might have just  been them lying they once again in  Florida are seeing record numbers of new  cases now I mentioned that the cases are  dramatically shifting from some parts of  the country to others this doesn't mean  you know Kings aren't going terribly  everywhere I am thrilled to say that  here in Massachusetts at least for now  cases have been very steadily declining  since late April the graph I'm showing  you you'll see a one-day spike about a  week ago that's not really a spike that  that was a bunch of presumptive cases  from the three months of coronavirus  were all added in on that day but we are  looking really good here and I'm  thrilled to see that so this is a story  not just about the virus itself which is  still raging with no treatment or  vaccine but it's a media story as well  about the agenda-setting power that  corporate media has we said six save  seven weeks ago Trump's strategy is  going to be just start pretending it  doesn't exist start talking about the  economy jobs reopening and a bunch of  corporate media has played along now in  the meantime things are so bad here in  the United States with coronavirus that  as more and more countries or reopening  travel the United States is being banned  I'll give you an example Iceland has so  dominated the virus that Iceland decided  that on I believe it's June 15th they're  going to reopen tourism when you get to  Iceland you have to have a kovat test at  the airport or quarantine for 14 days  people are going to be able to 